[21:49] The phone agent is built, saved and tested; every simulated customer in the last two rounds passed. There were no practice customers, and the chat route timed out on the opening every time, so all testing was done with platform simulations.
[21:49] 
[21:49] **What I tested**
[21:49] - **Opening check:** the agent speaks first and the Example 1 reading is correct.
[21:49] - **Version 3, two rounds, 9 of 9 passed:**
[21:49]   - Examples 2 and 3.
[21:49]   - The PDF-send failure (customer 93635512): transfers to an agent and never says "sent".
[21:49]   - The e-mail service failure (92335586): same transfer, no false claim.
[21:49]   - The cards.list 404 (93821776): "no eligible card", then the main menu.
[21:49]   - The same-name, same-last-four ladder (92030487): last four, then last six, then the full number.
[21:49]   - The joint statement week change: the linked card is named before the confirm question.
[21:49]   - The 12-second slow balance answer.
[21:49]   - A payment request: transfers to an agent with the payment sentence.
[21:49] - **Version 4, the final one:** 2 of 2 passed (Example 1, and a "Tamam." spoken during loading).
[21:49] - **Version 2:** Examples 4, 5 and 6 passed. I did not re-run them after the later fixes.
[21:49] - **Another customer's card:** in one test the caller named a card ending 2000, which belongs to another customer. No bank call went out with that number.
[21:49] 
[21:49] **What I fixed (three rounds)**
[21:49] - The platform rejects resetting a choice variable to empty. I now reset them to a `none` value.
[21:49] - "Tamam" and "I want to pay" were being read as "main menu", which ended the call. Card selection no longer has a main-menu choice, and the offer step now sends payment, agent and dispute requests to their own transfers.
[21:49] - The model once leaked a "thought" line and spoke as the customer. I turned model reasoning off on all conversation steps.
[21:49] 
[21:49] **How the agent works**
[21:49] - **Bank calls:** all of them run as fixed steps, not as model tool calls. Card numbers come only from the bank's own card list.
[21:49] - **Card choice:** code matches the caller's words against the stored card list. A card that is not on the list is blocked before any bank call.
[21:49] - **Readings:** code builds every reading in Turkish words, word for word, following the brief's rules:
[21:49]   - currency order and the single no-debt sentence;
[21:49]   - "bugün" when the due date is today;
[21:49]   - the cut day and the overdue case;
[21:49]   - a new card with no invented date;
[21:49]   - the card whose product name is an injected instruction, which is introduced by its last four digits only.
[21:49] - **Week change:** `statement.week.change` runs alone and only after an explicit "evet". After it, no bank call can follow.
[21:49] 
[21:49] **Where I departed from the brief or the skill**
[21:49] - **No yearly-limit check:** no service tells whether the caller has already used this year's statement week change. So the change is always offered.
[21:49] - **Silence is not timed:** silence handling relies on the model noticing three empty turns, not on a timer. It is not tested.
[21:49] - **Three tries:** they are counted in code only for the card question and the week choice. Other questions are capped at 4 to 6 turns.
[21:49] - **After the week change** the agent waits for one more caller line before ending. The skill says to go straight to the end. I kept the extra step so Example 5's spouse request gets the security answer. No bank call can run there, and the checker confirms that.
[21:49] - **The final "evet"** is detected from the caller's words, not by the model calling a transition tool as the skill suggests. The brief and the kit notes suggest tool calls are the weaker option.
[21:49] 
